1
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:13,360
Try leaving peace behind,
lightly, and step away.

2
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,880
aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa.

3
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:34,000
I kick a pebble and my shoes fly off too.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,240
So, to the head carpenter
whose savings I'd been keeping,

5
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

6
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I leave some of my energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:56,800
Katsushika, no good,
even yawns are an emergency.

8
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:02,540
The one unchanged
streetscape is strangely kind.

9
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:10,420
From the water intake
tower with its pointed cap,

10
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:16,800
the sunset falls toward the vast sky.

11
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:25,260
Why does tomorrow have to end too?

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,060
You can only win.
Again, happiness, they say.

13
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
I only realized it after losing it.

14
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,040
Because I'm such a fool.

15
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,760
Bodyguard of love.

16
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:56,220
The special plane carrying
King Edinburu's family

17
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:59,080
has just arrived at Narita Airport.

18
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:03,120
The King and Queen are now disembarking.

19
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:07,900
Their beloved daughter, Princess Fanny,
is visiting Japan for the first time.

20
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,280
Here in front of the Akasaka Guest House,
where they will be staying.

21
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:18,260
The car carrying the King's family
is expected to arrive shortly.

22
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:24,360
Along the route to the Guest House, 500
police officers are providing tight security.

23
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:29,240
In an emergency, orders from headquarters
are received through the earpiece receiver,

24
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:31,700
enabling a swift response.

25
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:34,380
Bottom of the ninth, two outs,
runner on first, with the score 1–0.

26
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:36,480
The batter is Takahashi,
who still hasn't gotten a hit today.

27
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,720
The King's car is coming into view.

28
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,760
The pitcher winds up and
throws the first pitch.

29
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:49,940
He's been shot!

30
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:53,400
What? Stop the car!

31
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:53,840
What happened?

32
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:00,100
Damn, this is bad.
Things have gotten out of hand.

33
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:04,080
Ryo-san, if it was a mistake,
you'd better apologize quickly.

34
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:07,940
Ryo-chan, what on earth happened?

35
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:10,820
Well, I didn't do anything, I swear.

36
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:12,120
What is this?

37
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,340
Any moment now,
he'll hit a walk-off home run

38
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,520
Toshio Takahashi

39
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:21,000
So the hit was a home run, then?

40
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,300
That's right.

41
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:25,820
Sorry, it seems my
subordinate misunderstood.

42
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:32,480
Honestly, Takahashi is a real headache.

43
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,300
Bakabon!

44
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:39,280
What do you think national
security preparations are, anyway?

45
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,980
Lime, nothing went wrong here,
so it's fine, isn't it!

46
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:44,680
Your day off tomorrow is cancelled!

47
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:48,160
Eeeeeh, I don't want that!

48
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,500
We've arrived safely.

49
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:02,460
It seems Japan isn't as
safe as it used to be.

50
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:06,440
Tomorrow's personal security
will surely be tight again.

51
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,600
What's wrong, Fanny?

52
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:12,400
Because even without them,

53
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,340
with the security people right beside me,

54
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:16,920
my private schedule just isn't any fun.

55
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:20,280
Fanny, you're still such a child.

56
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:22,020
I'm an adult already.

57
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:23,360
Because tomorrow...

58
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:27,140
Your Majesty, there's been a slight
change to tomorrow's official schedule.

59
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:28,420
Understood.

60
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,180
Mother, tomorrow...

61
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:34,780
Tomorrow's dress alterations are finished.

62
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:36,020
Coming!

63
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:40,400
Bunny, don't trouble the attendants.
Be a good girl.

64
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:48,080
Everyone's completely
forgotten about my birthday.

65
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:54,200
Bunny-sama, where are you going?

66
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,180
Princess, move!

67
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:56,060
It's the restroom!

68
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:15,000
Princess Bunny will make an unofficial
visit to this Katsushika Wonderland.

69
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,280
The visit will last thirty minutes.

70
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:21,180
So that under no circumstances will the
princess be put in danger during that time,

71
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:24,260
we must maintain the utmost vigilance.

72
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:28,140
Just when it's supposed to be unofficial,
I'm stuck babysitting a brat?

73
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:29,500
Ryo-san,

74
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:30,220
What?

75
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:35,100
You're here to make up
for yesterday's screw-up.

76
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:43,820
If I catch you listening to baseball this time,
you're fired, got it?

77
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,500
I understand.

78
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:51,640
We've received a request to avoid heavy-handed security,
since it's an amusement park.

79
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:56,620
So we'll discreetly guard her
without the general public noticing.

80
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:06,600
Yeah, with this, no one will notice us.

81
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,040
It looks kind of weak.
And it's hard to move in.

82
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,480
Don't call it a "mansion"!

83
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:17,540
Chief, it suits you way too well.

84
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:22,340
Okay, everyone, are you ready?

85
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:26,320
I asked someone from Wonderland
to teach us the moves.

86
00:06:26,940 --> 00:06:27,960
There's really such a thing?

87
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,980
First, the basic greeting.

88
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:34,420
Spread your arms out like this,

89
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:37,200
Welcome to Wonderland!

90
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,940
Next, the pose for when
someone asks you to take a photo.

91
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:43,360
The key is to lightly place
a hand toward the guest.

92
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:46,600
And this is the bye-bye
pose for when they leave.

93
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,200
Watch the movement of the bridge.

94
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:50,580
You expect us to do that?

95
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:52,200
Ryo-san, Ryo-san.

96
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,560
The hello pose

97
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,080
The photo pose

98
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,420
Bye-bye-bye-bye

99
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:01,200
Really get into character

100
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,700
Any questions?

101
00:07:04,420 --> 00:07:08,260
Teacher, question: if there's a cheeky kid,
can we smack them?

102
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:11,040
Absolutely not. You'd go flying.

103
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:12,358
But once,

104
00:07:12,408 --> 00:07:16,220
I saw a drunk hugging
the princess in a parade,

105
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:19,060
do we just pretend not to see even then?

106
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:21,179
In such cases,

107
00:07:21,229 --> 00:07:23,969
a character like this gives a stern warning.

108
00:07:24,019 --> 00:07:27,100
Idol characters must
not lay a hand on anyone.

109
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,080
I see.

110
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:30,028
When taking photos with guests,

111
00:07:30,078 --> 00:07:33,640
Can we ask for her number if she's pretty?

112
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:37,700
That sleepy-looking guy who was
hitting on those seven men before

113
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:42,200
Then how many Tsukki Bears
are in this amusement park?

114
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:46,360
I have a feeling there are about ten,
going by my instinct.

115
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,080
Very well, let me answer.

116
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:54,200
Tsukki Bear is one, and only one,
in each of your hearts.

117
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,220
Then how many female ones are there?

118
00:07:57,220 --> 00:07:59,940
You're not female, you're Nii-nii Bear.

119
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:02,220
And stop calling me Hikki, Hikki.

120
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:02,559
Question.

121
00:08:02,609 --> 00:08:06,896
Prince Philip from Torando was partying
at a foreigner bar in Roppongi, but

122
00:08:06,946 --> 00:08:08,260
is that really okay?

123
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:11,700
Torando is a world of dreams and fantasy.

124
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,980
Don't go checking only
those kinds of places.

125
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:15,780
Yes, understood.

126
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,320
Well then, bye-bye.

127
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,640
That teacher's movements
are just like a manga.

128
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:27,620
Wow!

129
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:30,040
How wonderful!

130
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:36,380
We'll come to collect you in 30 minutes.

131
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:37,740
I understand.

132
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,280
At last, I'm free!

133
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:49,200
Hey, babe, wanna hang out with us?

134
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,320
You came alone, right?

135
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,700
Come on, what's the harm?

136
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,060
But I...

137
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:55,960
Let's have some fun.

138
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,040
What's this?

139
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,180
Bye-bye.

140
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:04,200
Sukki, are you going to protect me?

141
00:09:04,660 --> 00:09:05,380
Yeah, yeah.

142
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:10,080
So you're my bodyguards here. How nice!

143
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,938
The one inside is,

144
00:09:12,988 --> 00:09:15,726
if she finds out it's nothing
but sweaty middle-aged old men,

145
00:09:15,776 --> 00:09:17,480
she'll be pretty shocked, won't she.

146
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:19,300
It's Azules!

147
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,780
Stay here in droves, will you!

148
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:22,980
Shut up! Get lost!

149
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:26,260
I don't have time to deal with you!
You brats!

150
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:30,060
What do you think all this security is for!

151
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:33,640
You have to handle all of that while also
using polite speech with the princess.

152
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:35,260
Goo

153
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:37,240
Welcome to Wonderland!

154
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:40,060
Welcome to Wonderland!

155
00:09:40,060 --> 00:09:41,300
Jo-san, your feet are backwards!

156
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:45,440
They'll notice!

157
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:55,140
Welcome!

158
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:59,100
Tsukki looks fun! Let's ride that one!

159
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,020
Hurry, hurry!

160
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:09,300
Everyone, follow me!

161
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,220
That was fun.

162
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:19,300
Now, that one!

163
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:28,660
Next, this one!

164
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:36,520
Aaaaaaah!

165
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,900
Aaaaaaah!

166
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:41,640
That was fun.

167
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,520
At your age, you only have
yourself to blame for overdoing it.

168
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:50,460
Never mind about me.

169
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,480
Don't take your eyes off the princess.

170
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:54,360
It's a parade!

171
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:15,840
Rumors that a princess is visiting
have spread to the public, too.

172
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:18,620
We need to be especially
careful during the parade.

173
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:22,700
If she's that important, why not just lock
her in her room and keep her from going out?

174
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,480
Wow, how cute!

175
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:28,680
We didn't have security like that.

176
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,880
Stop the checkpoints!

177
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,180
Hey, who the hell are you?

178
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:36,800
What?

179
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:38,020
Whoa!

180
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:41,360
Who are you people? Get away from her!

181
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:43,040
Help!

182
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:45,560
Ryotsu! What's wrong, Ryotsu?

183
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:46,200
I wonder...!

184
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:48,880
This way!

185
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:54,500
Those people tried to kidnap me!

186
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,520
What? For now,
let's head back to headquarters!

187
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,280
No! If we go back, we'll be caught!

188
00:11:59,020 --> 00:11:59,880
What's going on?

189
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:32,180
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

190
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:32,280
Over there!

191
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:34,340
Tsukkin!

192
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,480
No one's here. Over there!

193
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:47,480
Maybe we should leave the
amusement park for a bit.

194
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:48,340
Right.

195
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:51,180
What's wrong?

196
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:55,480
Sorry. But Tsukkin suddenly
turned into a gorilla!

197
00:12:55,860 --> 00:12:57,180
Sorry for being a gorilla, then.

198
00:12:58,480 --> 00:12:59,420
N-no way.

199
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:02,860
We only went to pick up the princess!

200
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:04,040
What is the meaning of this?

201
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,860
Officer Ryotsu,

202
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:07,900
hand the princess over to the
bodyguards who came to collect her.

203
00:13:07,900 --> 00:13:09,780
Did you not hear those orders?

204
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:12,400
Ryotsu, Ryotsu, do you copy?

205
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,560
If you can hear me, respond.

206
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:17,280
Bring Princess Bunny back with you.

207
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,680
Ryotsu, Ryotsu.

208
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:19,300
That's enough.

209
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:22,260
We'll take it from here.

210
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:25,760
The kidnapper is fleeing
with Princess Bunny.

211
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:28,180
Wait, we didn't kidnap her, please wait!

212
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:31,280
He's not the kind of man
who would do such a thing.

213
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:32,380
That's right.

214
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:34,580
Restrain him the moment you find him.

215
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:37,280
If necessary,
shooting him may be unavoidable.

216
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:00,100
A phone! Is there a phone?

217
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:03,320
Damn, of all times to
leave my cell phone behind!

218
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:04,600
Hey, look!

219
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:06,760
There's the Eiffel Tower!

220
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:10,980
That's Tokyo Tower.
We have to tell the Chief quickly.

221
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:13,880
And over there, the Golden Gate Bridge!

222
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:16,410
That's the Rainbow Bridge.

223
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:19,000
This is no time for sightseeing in Tokyo!

224
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,960
Where's a public phone?

225
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:22,160
No way.

226
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:25,920
Right. It'd be faster to grab a taxi
and head straight to the station.

227
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:28,160
Because you're the kidnapper, after all.

228
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:33,360
Those pirates... are they the
bodyguards who came to pick me up?

229
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:39,620
I'm sorry.

230
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:41,100
I want no part of this.

231
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:42,980
What on earth have you done?

232
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:44,420
What's going to happen to me?

233
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:45,060
Am I getting fired?

234
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:46,540
Definitely fired, no doubt about it.

235
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:47,960
Tsukki!

236
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:48,620
Nice work.

237
00:14:48,620 --> 00:14:50,160
I'll flag down a taxi for you,

238
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,780
so go back to the station on your own.

239
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:52,560
Got it?

240
00:14:53,380 --> 00:14:54,500
Hey, taxi!

241
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:56,540
I don't want to go home yet.

242
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:59,800
I want to stay like this a little longer.

243
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:01,880
I also want to learn
more about this country.

244
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:04,580
If you grant my request,

245
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:05,740
I'll definitely reward you.

246
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:07,560
A reward

247
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:08,320
Yes.

248
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,980
I am the princess of the Kingdom of Edinbur.

249
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:14,720
O-oh, I see.

250
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:19,820
Princess equals rich people
equals rewards pouring in!

251
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:26,180
Understood. Especially since it's a
request from Princess Bunny herself.

252
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:27,060
Really?

253
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:29,600
I'm so happy.

254
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:40,260
Lovely. Thanks, Tsukki.

255
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:43,320
I'm not Tsukki. I'm Ryotsu Kankichi.

256
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:44,480
Kankiri?

257
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:47,120
Not Kankiri. Kankichi.

258
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:50,440
You made the right choice
picking me as your tour guide.

259
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:52,960
Though I only specialize
in the old downtown areas.

260
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,680
This is the town where I was born.

261
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,200
Asakusa, the best in all of Japan.

262
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,520
Kankichi was born in Asakusa?

263
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:12,540
Kankichi.

264
00:16:13,460 --> 00:16:16,560
There are lots of foreign tourists around here,
so I won't stand out, right?

265
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:41,140
Look, what a cute doll.

266
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:45,500
It's delicious.

267
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:49,040
Can you eat this?

268
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:52,760
It's sweet.

269
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,400
If you eat it, you have to pay.

270
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:55,420
Me?

271
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:00,040
What, you don't have any money at all?

272
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:04,000
What, and you're a princess?

273
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,700
These are salted beans.

274
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:17,380
They're a luxury,
so we rarely got to eat them as kids.

275
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:22,660
You're so clumsy.

276
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:23,880
Like this.

277
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,320
There's also this way.

278
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:41,480
There are all kinds of other ways to eat them,
you know.

279
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:51,800
It's Asakusa's Kannon-sama.

280
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:54,060
You should make a wish to it.

281
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:55,640
What about Kankichi?

282
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:00,540
When I was a kid,
I begged it to make me rich.

283
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:02,520
But it still hasn't granted it, has it?

284
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:09,820
Does a princess like you have
any wishes she wants granted?

285
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:13,800
I hope I become an ordinary girl from a normal family,
not a princess.

286
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:19,240
Today is my birthday.

287
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,480
Birthday.

288
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,040
I've always been alone.

289
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,100
Instead of my father or my mother,

290
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:30,640
I had Uba, Jijo and S.P. with me, though.

291
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:38,900
Not one person understood how I felt.

292
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:48,520
My family was poor,

293
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:53,980
and my old man and mom were
always scolding and hitting me.

294
00:18:54,380 --> 00:18:57,220
How many times did I beg them to
adopt me out to another family?

295
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:01,680
So I thought someone like
you wouldn't have any troubles.

296
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:05,920
You've completely forgotten my birthday.

297
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:08,940
I turned twenty today, you know.

298
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:11,960
Alright, then, as a birthday treat,

299
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:14,780
how about we stretch our legs to the Fukagawa festival,
Princess?

300
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:17,100
I'll accompany you, Prince Citrus.

301
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:19,520
Are you all right, Lady Funny?

302
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:25,980
Hyan!

303
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:27,880
Wh-wait, hold on!

304
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,340
Get out of the way!

305
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:35,360
Takichi!

306
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:58,820
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

307
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:01,840
This is the venue for Princess
Bunny's birthday party.

308
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:03,020
What's wrong?

309
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:06,000
We've been keeping it a secret
from the princess for today.

310
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:10,980
Apparently the king and queen and the Japanese
Prime Minister have been preparing the party.

311
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:13,580
Apparently the princess isn't feeling well.

312
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:17,080
I hear the party's start time
will be pushed back a little.

313
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,320
Will she be all right?

314
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:20,000
Kankichi, I...

315
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,020
That's good

316
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,400
Kankichi!

317
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:26,520
Bunny!

318
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:32,220
Ryo-san

319
00:20:32,220 --> 00:20:33,620
Don't move, Ryotsu!

320
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:37,700
Well then, let's go.

321
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:40,520
Their Majesties are very worried about you.

322
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:43,580
Brave No.

323
00:20:43,580 --> 00:20:47,760
I insisted that this
man show me around Tokyo.

324
00:20:48,260 --> 00:20:49,180
Step back.

325
00:20:51,220 --> 00:20:53,320
It is an honor to have been of service.

326
00:20:57,120 --> 00:20:59,000
I caused everyone a lot of worry,

327
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:01,940
but today has been the best day of my life.

328
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:04,040
Thank you, Kankichi.

329
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:07,720
Princess Bunny, your car is here.

330
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:08,920
Understood.

331
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:15,240
Your Highness.

332
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:19,000
Here, a souvenir of Tokyo.

333
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:19,560
Thank you.

334
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:23,240
Also, the Fukagawa festival
is held every month,

335
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:24,040
so someday again.

336
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:29,760
Goodbye.

337
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:49,860
Happy birthday, Princess Bunny!

338
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:13,160
That wild girl has finally gone

339
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:16,440
So you were in charge of
escorting the princess, senpai?

340
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:19,620
In the end, we didn't even get a thank-you.

341
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:21,540
All that hard work and no reward!

342
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:22,360
Ryotsu, are you here?

343
00:22:23,740 --> 00:22:25,580
Bunny-san sent something for you.

344
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:27,460
From Bunny-san? To me?

345
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:33,800
A doll?

346
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:37,120
Bunny-san, during this security detail,

347
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:39,260
seems to have taken a real liking to Ryotsu.

348
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:41,520
The station chief was pleased, too.

349
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:43,300
And the disciplinary
action has been called off.

350
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:45,020
Good for you, Ryotsu.

351
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:49,940
There's a letter attached to the card.

352
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:50,880
What is it?

353
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:51,000
What?

354
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:54,555
My bodyguard, Kankichi.

355
00:22:54,605 --> 00:22:56,672
Thank you for a wonderful birthday.

356
00:22:56,722 --> 00:22:59,940
Please come visit Edinburgh someday.

357
00:23:00,600 --> 00:23:02,942
This time, I'll be your guide.

358
00:23:02,992 --> 00:23:05,200
With love from Fanny.

359
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:09,020
"With love," how nice, Ryo-san.

360
00:23:09,700 --> 00:23:11,620
So she's fallen for me, Fanny.

361
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:14,180
Well then, I'm off!

362
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,940
Ryotsu! You're not seriously planning to go to Edinburgh,
are you?

363
00:23:17,940 --> 00:23:18,935
Come on, senpai,

364
00:23:18,985 --> 00:23:22,120
I think that was just a polite formality.

365
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:25,280
Commoners, please be quiet.

366
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:27,940
Next time we meet, I'll be Prince Kankitsu.

367
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:30,180
When I visit Japan again,
I'm counting on the security staff.

368
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:31,480
Bye-bye!

369
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,420
This is serious!

370
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:38,300
Princess Fanny of Edinburgh,
who recently visited Japan,

371
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:40,140
has announced her engagement.

372
00:23:40,980 --> 00:23:44,700
Her fiancé is the prince of a neighboring country,
long rumored.

373
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:47,480
So it really was just a polite formality.

374
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:50,520
She left this behind.

375
00:23:52,700 --> 00:23:54,800
What a complete idiot.

376
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:57,000
Just you wait, seriously!

377
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:00,020
My beloved Prince Kankichi, I'm coming now!

378
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:23,700
With surprise and commotion,
with spirit and resolution, swiftly erased

379
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:35,480
decided, with flashes of inspiration,
bouncing, gathering, into action, flying away

380
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:40,060
Above all, an incredible power

381
00:24:40,330 --> 00:24:46,100
Gather everyone, if you come here

382
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:52,400
A dreamlike, final energy

383
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:56,800
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday

384
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,720
Drawing across the sky,
standing on the ground

385
00:24:59,720 --> 00:25:03,440
The star of Kameari is coming,
and it's a wonder, you know

386
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:07,160
This should be fine, right?

387
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:08,680
Like hell it's fine!

388
00:25:21,820 --> 00:25:25,880
Orion, the movie theater that's bringing
the curtain down on a long history

389
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:29,460
There were memories of my childhood there

390
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:31,860
Back when movies were
the king of entertainment

391
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:37,660
Next time: Asakusa Cinema Paradise,
see you then

